# .worktreeinclude — the gitignored files a fresh worktree of this repository needs.
# Claude Code reads it when it creates a worktree, and so does `wt`. A pattern copies a file
# only when it matches and is gitignored, so nothing tracked is ever duplicated. A pattern with
# no slash, or one opening with **/, matches at any depth, which is what reaches each package
# directory's own env files and local settings.
.env*
**/.claude/settings.local.json
# Nothing under node_modules: a dependency can ship a local settings file of its own, and copying
# it would create a node_modules that stops each directory's install-if-missing guard.
!**/node_modules/**
